{
  "_comment": [
    "sg13g2-bandgap -- `klt sim` request template for closed-loop-psrr-pex",
    "(issue #278). Instantiated by run_klt_sim.sh per (process, supply)",
    "variant, exactly like the vref bench: the PWL ramp target is baked per",
    "supply and the runner image's single-models.lib channel carries one",
    "process per request (klayout-tools#2668). 15 requests of 3 temperatures",
    "each, merged deterministically before the adapter.",
    "",
    "The declared analysis is the AC sweep; the bench body's own `.control`",
    "block runs the settle transient first and then the same AC sweep (see",
    "the body's header for why), so klt's re-run of the declared analysis",
    "re-solves an identical operating point and the top-level `.meas ac`",
    "cards below attach to it.",
    "",
    "The four request-level measurements are LINEAR magnitudes (|v(vref)|),",
    "not dB: a resident-vector `.save` list disables `par('...')` in `.meas`",
    "find (ngspice 46), so the dB conversion happens in the enrichment pass",
    "over single reported values -- a unit conversion, not a differencing,",
    "so the 6-s.f. disposition is not spent. The op-point columns and the",
    "worst-case/frequency columns come from the per-corner log (body-side",
    "meas cards and the print table)."
  ],
  "engine": "ngspice",
  "netlist": "@@BODY@@",
  "netlist_source": "extracted",
  "models": { "lib": "@@CORNER_BUNDLE@@" },
  "corners": {
    "process": ["typ", "bcs", "wcs", "sf", "fs"],
    "temperature_c": [-40, 27, 125]
  },
  "analysis": { "kind": "ac", "args": "dec 30 1 1e9" },
  "measurements": [
    { "name": "psrr_dc_lin", "spice": ".meas ac psrr_dc_lin find v(vref) at=1" },
    { "name": "psrr_1khz_lin", "spice": ".meas ac psrr_1khz_lin find v(vref) at=1k" },
    { "name": "psrr_100khz_lin", "spice": ".meas ac psrr_100khz_lin find v(vref) at=100k" },
    { "name": "psrr_1mhz_lin", "spice": ".meas ac psrr_1mhz_lin find v(vref) at=1meg" }
  ],
  "options": {
    "timeout_s": 900,
    "keep_artifacts": true
  }
}
